        <p>THE BENEFITS OF SCIENCE.</p>
        <p>- It is seldom thet any discovery of uience is such as will benifit all classes of people. S ene ot thr greatest discoveries of the age, while they have prove q directly beniiel ato thousands, have also, at least for a time, injneed other thee-Tare-ie. Fven some of the best nsedicinal preparations, however much they reay do to remove one class of disease. or euit some consritutiens, at the same time either deepen the hold of another dis- use, or leave it entirely untouched, or if they benefit one elass of patients, they may injure another. Now the zreat need of the age is some ecientifically arranged pre— paration which will cope effectua.lly with the prevalent diseataps of this country,which will be certain tO do good when fairly tried, which will be equally adapted to the needs of the merchant and the worknaan,the professional sun, and he who wins his bread by the sweat of his brow, the student, the clerk,the factory hand,the miner, and the roadside labourer. It should be, too, such a preparation as contains no injurious ingredients, and which may be taken with impunity by the weakly child, or the delicate lady, as well as by the stronger constituted man. Such a discovery would deserve to be called The Perfection of Medicinal Prenaratiene, and would indeed be an Invaluable boon to Suffering Humanity. Now this much needed boon has been found, has been tried, and wherever proved, it has been found satisfactory. We refer to Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters, the Vegetable Tonic, which when once tried has been always recommended, and has proved success- ful when all other medicine has failed to give relief, and we may say further, that it has proved permanently beneficial, when other preparations at best only give temporary relief. It is strongly recemmended as The Best Remedy of the Age for Endiges:ion in its different forms, such as Sick Headache, Pains in the Side, Giddi- ness, Loss of Appetite, also for Nervousness and Nervous Disorders, Sleeplessness, Neuralgia, Lew Spirits, and all kinds of Weakness. It has often proved very beneficial to persons suffering from great Weakness, either after an iilness, long confinement to ill-ventilated rooms, or any ether cause. It strikes at the source of the Disease, removing the cause cf the illness, and strengthens those parts of the eystem which have been weakened by it, and therefore most liable to colds and other ailments. Gwilym Evans' Quinine Bitters being purely vegetable, it is. a Natural Tonic.and suited to all ages at all seasons of the year. It is everywhere acknowledged to he a powerful aid in restoring the body to a healthy state when deranged by disease. If you suspect that your health is beginning to fail, brace up your nerves, and fortify your ccnstitution by taking now a course of this excellent Tonic, which is sold everywhere iv betties at 2s 91 and Is 61 each, but should any difficulty be ex- perienced in precuriog it, the Proprietors will forward same for the above prices, carriage free. Avoid Imita- tions. When purehasing,see the came,' Gwilym Evans," en Libel, Stamp, and Bottle. Sole Proprietors: Quinine Bitters Manufacturing Company, Limited, Llanelly, South Wales.</p>
