      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-11-24_WidnesExaminer_art0099" n="art0099">
        <head>EDWARD WILLIAM PRINGLE.</head>
        <p>EDWARD WILLIAM PRINGLE.</p>
        <p>Every year as Scott's Emulsion becomes better known, it increases in popularity as a remedy for bronebitis and coughs and for all affections of throat and lungs. 'the soothing and healing proper- ties of Scott's Emulsion, together with its power to give strength and vitality to the system, make it especially adapted to the treatment of tkese fami- liar maladies. The reason bronchitis becomes chronic is because the system is too weak to resist it. Let us give yJu an illustration of the favourable opinion hold of Scott's Emulsion by those who have used it : " Primrose Bank, Hawarden, "February 2nd, 1899.</p>
        <p>"Dear Sirs,—Wbeu three weeks old, my little boy had bronchitis very badly, which left bim with a very weak chest, causing great anxiety to both his father and myself. Att'r trying all sorts of remedies, we were recommended ' Scott's Emulsion, which I am sure saYei his life, m thing him quite a different boy. This winter both my children had a bad attack of whooping</p>
        <p>ALL COUNTRYi4PROPLE should read The Rural World H. weekly, which contains articles on Horses, Cattle, the Dairy, Poultry, Bees, Rabbits, Pigs, Gardening, Natural History, Botany of the Farm and Garden, the Home, Foreign rid Colonial Intelligence, Answers to Correspondents, etc. It is profusely illustrated, and is, altogether, a most interest- ing and instructive farming and country paper. A good medium for servants requiring situations. The Manager if-re to send a specimen copy free. The address is 110 and 11 STRAND, Loadm, W. C.—Advt.</p>
        <p>(From a photograph.)</p>
        <p>cough and could keep nothing down but half to one teaspoonft4l of Scolt's Emulsion. They are new in the best o' health. I cannot speak ton highly of Scott's Emulsios,and I shall in the future, as in the past, recommend it at every opportunity. Yours faithfully, "(Signed) (Mits.) R. W. hansom" The reason Scott's Emulsion in so effectual is be- cause it is a form of cod-liver oil which requires almost no digestive effort, combined with bypophos- phites and glycerine. Auutlier great advantage of Scott's Emulsion is that it is co palatable that children do not look upon it as a medicine. This makes its administration easy. Adults can take Scott's Emulsion without aversion, and it is as bene- ficial tu them as it is to children. _</p>
        <p>You can obtain a sample of Scutt's Emulsion by sendieg threepence to cover postage to Scott and B)wee, Limited, Manufacturing Chemists, 95, Great Saffron Hill, Landon, E.C., and mentioning this paper. All chemists sell Scott's Emulsion.</p>
        <p>A. TllompsoN,. ESTATE, HOUSE,</p>
        <p>AND INSURANCH AGENT.</p>
        <p>100, BEWSEY-R)AD, WARRINGTON. PROPERTY BOUGHT AND SOLD. REASONABLE TER MS.</p>
