      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1899-11-24_WidnesExaminer_art0109" n="art0109">
        <head>VACCINATION.</head>
        <p>VACCINATION.</p>
        <p>Warrington Magistrates Refuse Exemptions.</p>
        <p>At the Warrington Police Court on Friday, a gentleman named Ward, who resides in Battersby- lane, applied to the magistrates, the Mayor (Alder- man Roberts), Alderman Wright, Councillor t"msthurst and Ar. Elepherd for an order exempting his two children from vaccination.</p>
        <p>The Mayor (Alderman Roberts) asked the appli- cant if he was in the town at the time of the small- pox epidemic, and on receiving a reply in the nega- tive, said that as deputy-chairman of the Health Committee and an active member at the time, and as a result of his experience he did not feel dis- posed to grant any exemptions from vaccination. They had been unable to cope with the email-pox epidemic until the inhabitants of the town had been re-vaccinated, and in proportion as that ob- tained the disease began to subside. Alderman Wright: That is quite true. Applicant said he objected to vaccination, and did not believe in it,</p>
        <p>The Mayor: It is not enough to ay that you don't believe in it. We have had a sad experience here.</p>
        <p>Applicant said he had a conscientious objection. The Mayor. On what ground? That is not enough. lam not disposed to grant exemptions. The other magistrates can do as they like, Alderman Wright expressed a similar opinion, and left the Bench.</p>
        <p>The Mayor : What I saw in Warrington at the time of the small-pox epidemic is enough to last me all my life. lam very sorry, but personally I must decline to grant the application. His Worship then left the Bench.</p>
        <p>Mr. Hepherd said he could not grant the applica- tion, and also left the Bench.</p>
        <p>, Councillor Smethurst was the only =agistrate who remained.</p>
        <p>The Deputy Magistrates Clerk advised the appli- cant to come again when other magistrates were on the Bench.</p>
      </div>
