        <p>Each Club is numbered lor 2. Al space provided. If a draw is intended put X. -NOTE.—Don't cut the Coupon into strips, se-sd the complete form. This Competition is run in conjunction with the " Oompetition Key,"janCothec papers. NAME ADDRESS CONDITIONS. I.—The first coupon is free, and no competitor oan send in more tints one free coupon, Enclose Id. stamp for every othar coupon used. One Shinig Postal Order must be enclosed if all the coupons en above sheet are used Any number of coup ma an be sent In if paid for at the rate of One Shilling for each 20. 2.—Cross all Postal Orders and keep the numbers. 3.—No competitor can take more than one share of Vie £lO prize. 4.—The coupons must be forwarded to the lixaminer Offioe Warrington, the envelope to IN) endorsed Football Coupon," so as to be delivered by the first post on Thursday morning. If the envelope bears Wednesday's postmark, it will be received up to 5 p.m. on Thursday. Coupons delivered by hand must be received not later than 9 a.m. on Thursday. s.—Competitors demanding a scrutiny must enclose fee of Ten Shillings, give number of Postal Or r (if any), and num- ber of coupons sent. In the event of the claim proving correct the fee will be returned. 6.—ln the event of two or more competitors tying, prize money will be divided. 7.—A1l attempts in this competition must be made on coupons cut from this paper. B.—When not less than 40 attempts are made, the coupons of unsuccessful competitors for the coupon prize will be carried forward and added to ale number sent in, in the next competition,so that sooner or later the coupon prize must be won by regular competitors 9.—The results will appear in the first issue following the result of the matches. [RESULTS OF COMPETITI)N AND LIST OF WINNERS ON PAGE 5.]</p>
        <p>NESTLE'S .899 XMAS PRIZES. For the 58 Nearest Estimates of the number of Tins of Nestle's Milk sold through the Manchester Office . . During the year ending Wednesday noon, December 13th, 1899. Entries dose at 12 o'clock (noon) on Dec 13th. INSTRUCTION S.--Cut off that part of the label of a 1-lb Tin of Nestle's Milk across which the words "Prepared in Switzerland " are printed in red. (This can be easily done by drawing a knife down the Black Lines enclosing this part.) On the back of it, write your Estimate in Figures, with your Name and Address. NOTHING ELSE, PLEASE. BUT WRITE CLEARLY. Post it in all enve- lope (penny postago) addressed : "NESTLE'S COMPETITION," 63, CORPORATION STREET, MANCHESTER. N.B.—The Postal Authorities will not carry this for a Halfpenny. EMPLOYEES OF THE FIRM MAY NOT COMPETE. IN CASE OF TIES, PRIZES ,WILL BE DIVIDED.</p>
